{#
  The page's title block: one <h1>, at one size, with the page's primary
  action beside it (design.md §7.6).

  Before this partial the site's 106 <h1> used twenty different class
  combinations across three sizes, and the fourteen title-plus-action
  headers used four different flex skeletons — two neighbouring pages
  never gave their own name the same weight. The size chosen here (h3 on
  desktop via .h3, full width action stacking on mobile) is now the only
  one.

  Usage:
  {% include 'partials/page_header.html.twig' with {
      title: 'Mouvements',
      subtitle: 'Tous les mouvements du compte sélectionné.',  -- optional
      action_label: 'Nouvel article',   -- optional, with action_url
      action_url: '/news/new',          -- optional
      action_icon: 'bi-plus-lg',        -- optional, defaults to bi-plus-lg
  } only %}

  The action is the page's PRIMARY action — btn-primary, at most one per
  screen (design.md §7.4); creation actions always live here, never as a
  full-width band under the title and never in green. A page needing a
  second control next to its title probably needs a toolbar below it, not
  a second primary.
#}
<div class="d-flex flex-column flex-sm-row justify-content-between align-items-sm-center gap-2 mb-4 page-header">
    <div>
        <h1 class="h3 mb-0">{{ title }}</h1>
        {% if subtitle|default('') %}
            <p class="text-body-secondary small mb-0 mt-1">{{ subtitle }}</p>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
    {% if action_label|default('') and action_url|default('') %}
        <a href="{{ action_url }}" class="btn btn-primary w-100 w-sm-auto flex-shrink-0">
            <i class="bi {{ action_icon|default('bi-plus-lg') }}" aria-hidden="true"></i> {{ action_label }}
        </a>
    {% endif %}
</div>
